|~ The verbs of errors [D97]. Each resides on `::qlang/error`, the kind
   every error is a value of: the error `!|` opens is `::error{…}`, or
   the tag of the site that refused stacked over it, and its walk passes
   `::error` on its way to the map, so a verb declared here reaches every
   error. ~|

:trail
  |~~ The path of the error [D85]: each step it passed, from the one
      that raised it, with the subject that step met and the steps
      skipped after it.

      ~("x" | add 1 !| trail | count | eq 1)
      ~("x" | add 1 | mul 2 !| trail | first | /skipped | eq ~(mul 2))
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:returns ::vec | /trail)

:explain
  |~~ The explanation of the error [D98]: the page of its site [D7],
      the doc of the tag it shows, which says what failed and holds the
      examples of the failure, then the error itself, so it prints as
      the page above the error.

      ~("x" | add 1 !| explain | doc | content | contains "must be a number")
      ~(!{:k 1} !| explain | doc | eq (::error | docs | first))
  ~~|
  ::verb~(:subject ::any | :returns ::explanation | {:doc (type | docs | first) :error /} | tag ::explanation)
